      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“activates the sense of body position or movement”) is not explicitly supported by the provided packet; the packet describes passive wrist movements and clinical assessment (Wrist Position Sense Test) but does not define proprioceptive stimuli in terms of “sense of body position or movement.”",
        "While the second sentence is supported (the study uses an “event-related design” where each proprioceptive stimulus is “passive wrist movement,” assessed with wrist position sense), the first sentence remains an unsupported generalization."
